rules.text:
1. Option: mandatory
No. STC-030-01-2507-2509-M
2. Batch creation example
POST http://{endpoint}/v3/{resource}/batch-create
The body contains all the objects to be created.
{
"resources":[
{.......
},
{......
}
]
}
3. Batch deletion example
POST http://{endpoint}/v3/{resource}/batch-delete
The body contains all objects to be deleted.
{
"resources": [id1,id2,id3,id4]
}
4. Batch Change Example
POST http://{endpoint}/v3/{resource}/batch-update
The body contains all objects that need to be updated.
{
"resources":[
{.......
},
{......
}
]
}
5. Return value
The returned information can be returned in the following scenarios:
All success or all failure status codes are consistent with those returned by single resource operations;
Partial success or partial failure returns a 207 status code;
Exceptional situations return a 5xx status code;
Asynchronous operations should return a status code of 202, and an interface for querying the operation status must be provided.
[TABLE: 7 rows]

1 Option: mandatory
No. QUE-040-01-2507-2507-M
The API for obtaining resource sets can return the total number of resources that meet the query conditions in the returned message. The impact on the interface performance needs to be evaluated. If the impact on the interface performance is great, it is recommended that an independent API be provided to return the total number of resources.
Since this specification takes effect, new interfaces must comply with this specification, and existing interfaces are optional.
